iMac 5K stitch: attach the right tile's plane on a modeset from an off crtc

Applies ON TOP of imac5k-stitch-layer-7.x.patch and
imac5k-stitch-hide-slave.patch.

When the crtc was off and a client turns it on with a new framebuffer in
one commit (Plymouth's reboot/shutdown splash after the compositor exits,
or any KMS client doing disable + SetCrtc), the left tile showed the
picture and the right tile stayed black: the splash logo was cut exactly
at the seam.

Two gaps in the stitch layer, both only on that path:

- dc_commit_streams() brings the new streams up with no planes; planes are
  attached by the update_planes_and_stream() calls in
  amdgpu_dm_commit_planes(). The stitch pushed the peer (right-tile)
  surface update only when plane_needs_flip, which needs an old fb. With
  the crtc off there is none, so the peer stream ran with no plane. Now
  the peer plane is attached on that path too, with only its scaling (no
  flip_addr/plane_info, since the root's were not filled for this index).
- The peer dc_plane_state takes its buffer address from afb->address at
  atomic check, which is still 0 for a framebuffer that has never been
  pinned. prepare_fb filled the address only for the root plane; it now
  fills the peer plane too when it is new.

A compositor never hits this (it flips, and a flip pushes the peer update
with the root's address), and neither does the fbdev restore (its fb was
pinned long before). A static splash never flips, so the right tile stayed
black until power-off.

Tested on the iMac18,3 (linux-omarchy 7.2.15): a KMS test client that
disables the crtc and then modesets onto a new dumb buffer (left half blue,
right half orange) showed the right half black before and orange after.

